    answer: "Yes. The Console moved off the `/console` prefix and dropped the region and typed-resource segments, so `/console/project-fra-68a1c2/auth/user-9f3d0b` is now `/projects/68a1c2/auth/users/9f3d0b`, and `/organization-{id}` is now `/organizations/{id}`. Old links are not broken: the server matches pre-2.0 paths and returns a 302 to the new equivalent. The one exception is a deep link to a single webhook, which lands on the webhooks list because Console IV has no per-webhook page."
  - question: "Why did Appwrite move from SvelteKit to TanStack?"
    answer: "Two reasons. React has deeper library coverage for the components a console needs, including data tables, virtualized lists, code editors, and charts. And coding agents write React far more reliably than Svelte, which matters when much of the code behind a 600-page documentation site and a large console is now written with agent assistance."
